Subject: [PATCH] fonts: use Windows candidate families for Simplified Han fallback

Windows resolves a missing Han glyph using the Han script selected from
content/accept/system locale, then probes an ordered list of actual families.
Linux currently asks Fontconfig with the unmodified locale; for English in the
supplied Windows set that chooses Malgun Gothic rather than Microsoft YaHei.

Select the upstream Windows Simplified Han list only for a Windows profile
and only when the existing locale policy resolves the missing Han glyph to
Simplified Han. Verify actual family names and glyph coverage. Existing faces
that already cover the glyph, other scripts, other Han locales, non-Windows
profiles and no-profile behavior retain their existing paths. Unavailable or
non-covering candidates fall through. No font metric, numeric glyph bound,
fontconfig file, profile/schema field or JavaScript API is replaced.

Reference: resources/fingerprints/raw/unlabelled-20260910T140818Z.json,
fonts.metrics: 76 right edges differ by 2 px in the 41-patch subject. A
separate Windows-profile control measured the right bound of 字 at 40 px:
38 for Malgun and 40 for YaHei, both with 40 px advances. This is a selector candidate, not a claim
that remaining raster/DirectWrite metric differences are resolved.

Primary source at Chromium79460ebecaa5625e57a5fb679a735659e73dc687:
- platform/fonts/win/font_fallback_win.cc:210-211,539-557 (candidate/script policy)
- platform/fonts/win/font_cache_skia_win.cc:159-175,284-294 (family then coverage)
- platform/text/layout_locale.cc:198-216,226-256 (Han locale/default)
Paths above are under third_party/blink/renderer/. Uses existing loader/IPC.

V1 compilation and V3 conformance remain required. Broader Windows fallback
and DirectWrite line-gap policy remain unresolved.
